{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pe1E6QKooTkQwTZuUReAht","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Ralph Progress Log\n2\tRotated: Mon May  4 00:43:02 CEST 2026\n3\tPrevious log archived to: archive/progress-2026-05-04-0043.txt\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t## Codebase Patterns\n7\t- Repo dir is named `US-001` (capitalized) → cannot run `create-next-app .` directly because npm rejects capital letters in package names. Workaround: scaffold into a temp dir (e.g. `/tmp/ai-lecturer-scaffold`), then copy files into the worktree (skip the inner `.git`), and set the package name in `package.json` manually.\n8\t- `shadcn@latest` (v4.x) emits Tailwind v4 / `base-nova` style by default — incompatible with a Tailwind v3 project. Use `shadcn@2.3.0` for v3-compatible init, or write `components.json` by hand.\n9\t- Tailwind v3 baseline = `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;` in `globals.css` + `tailwind.config.ts` with `content: [\"./src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mdx}\"]` + `postcss.config.js` with `tailwindcss` and `autoprefixer` plugins. Theme/token wiring belongs in US-002, not US-001.\n10\t- Design tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css` (canonical source from `claude/design/source/tokens.css`) and are imported at the top of `src/app/globals.css`. Tailwind utilities resolve through CSS vars, so changing a `--*` value at runtime updates Tailwind classes too.\n11\t- Theme/accent/density are switched by `data-theme` / `data-accent` / `data-density` attributes on `<html>` (defaults: `light` / `default` / `comfortable`). Selectors in tokens.css are scoped to `:root[data-theme=…]` etc. — adding new variants means adding a new `:root[data-…=\"…\"]` block, not a new file.\n12\t- Geist Sans + Mono are loaded via `next/font` (`geist/font/sans`, `geist/font/mono`) in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Their `.variable` classNames define `--font-geist-sans` / `--font-geist-mono`; tokens.css references those via `var(--font-geist-sans)` inside `--font-sans` / `--font-prose` / `--font-display`. Don't hardcode font names anywhere else.\n13\t- Playwright skill at `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/` ships without `node_modules`; run `npm install --no-audit --no-fund` inside it before first use. Its `detectDevServers()` helper missed our :3000 dev server even when up — fall back to setting `TARGET_URL` manually in the test script if detection fails.\n14\t- **Zod is pinned to v3** (`^3.25.x`) because `zod-to-json-schema` returns an empty object on Zod v4. Don't bump zod to v4 unless the `zod-to-json-schema` import also changes. (Zod v4 has a native `z.toJSONSchema()`, but our AC mandates the third-party lib.)\n15\t- **Vitest needs its own alias config.** `vitest.config.ts` must declare `resolve.alias = { '@': fileURLToPath(new URL('./src', import.meta.url)) }`. Vitest does NOT read `tsconfig.json#paths`. Next + `tsc` + `tsx` (used by `npm run build:schemas`) DO auto-pick it up.\n16\t- **Eslint config does not exempt `_`-prefixed unused vars.** For \"drop one field\" test fixtures, use `const broken: Partial<typeof obj> = { ...obj }; delete broken.field;` — destructuring with `_name` triggers `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` warnings.\n17\t- **Schema layout.** Source-of-truth Zod schemas live in two places: per-widget data shapes at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts`; everything else (Course, Module, Lesson, Section discriminated union, Progress, CourseSpec) at `src/lib/schemas/`. `SectionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', […])` over `'theory'|'quiz'|'code'|'demo'|'sandbox'|'custom'`. Adding a new widget = new folder under `src/widgets/<Name>/` + register a variant in `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` + add it to the `widgets` map in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts`. `npm run build:schemas` regenerates the committed `*.json` files in `src/widgets/schemas/`.\n18\t- **Filesystem helpers** live in `src/lib/server/` (server-only — never import from a `'use client'` module). `paths.ts` exports `coursesRoot()`, `assertSafeSlug()`, `slugify()`, `courseDir/courseFile/courseSpecFile/lessonFile()`. `atomic.ts` exports `atomicWriteJson(path, data)` (writes to `<path>.tmp` then `fs.rename`). `coursesRoot()` honours `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` env var (used in tests); production reads `path.join(process.cwd(), 'courses')`. Disk layout: `courses/<slug>/{course.json, course-spec.json, lessons/<lessonSlug>.json}`.\n19\t- **Next 16 route handlers + vitest.** Tests can import handlers directly from `src/app/api/.../route.ts` and call them with a synthesised `Request` and `{ params: Promise.resolve({...}) }` (Next 15+ wraps params in a Promise). `NextResponse.json()` returns a real `Response`, so `await res.json()` and `res.status` work in tests. Put the test file OUTSIDE `src/app/` (e.g. `src/lib/server/api.test.ts`) so Next doesn't try to compile it as a route — vitest's `include: 'src/**/*.test.ts'` still picks it up.\n20\t- **Slug rules.** `assertSafeSlug` rejects empty strings and any slug containing `/`, `\\`, or `..` (path-traversal protection). Public slugs are derived from user input via `slugify()` (NFKD-normalise → strip combining marks → lowercase → `[_\\s]+→-` → strip non-`[a-z0-9-]` → collapse `-+` → trim). Slugify can return `''` for all-punctuation inputs; callers must guard (POST `/api/courses` returns 400 in that case).\n21\t- **Pyodide worker singleton.** Web Workers are bundled by Turbopack via `new Worker(new URL('./worker.ts', import.meta.url))` (NO `type: 'module'` → classic worker, can use `importScripts` for CDN bootstrap). The worker file at `src/lib/pyodide/worker.ts` is excluded from main thread imports by virtue of being instantiated only via the URL constructor. Client hook lives at `src/lib/pyodide/client.ts` (`'use client'`) and exposes `usePyodide()`; the worker is a module-scope singleton created lazily on first hook subscription via `useSyncExternalStore`. Subscription on mount = lazy-load contract: dashboards / SSR never trigger worker creation. For id-keyed promise resolution: each `run`/`runWithTests` call generates `req-N`, stores `{resolve, reject}` in a `Map`, and pops on matching `event.data.id`. Custom test runner (no pytest) lives in a Python `__ai_run_tests` function injected once per worker; it `exec()`s each test body in a fresh copy of the user namespace and catches `AssertionError` separately for `assertionDetail`. Test results array shape: `[{name, passed, traceback?, assertionDetail?}]`.\n22\t- **CodeMirror 6 setup.** Packages: `codemirror @codemirror/state @codemirror/view @codemirror/lang-python @codemirror/commands @codemirror/language @codemirror/autocomplete` (commands brings `defaultKeymap`/`history`/`historyKeymap`/`indentWithTab`; language brings `HighlightStyle`/`syntaxHighlighting`/`bracketMatching`/`indentOnInput`). Theme via `EditorView.theme({...})` consuming our `--code-bg/--code-text/--code-keyword/...` CSS vars. Highlight via `HighlightStyle.define([{ tag: t.keyword, color: 'var(--code-keyword)' }, ...])` from `@lezer/highlight` tags. Editor instantiated once in `useEffect(() => {...}, [])` with `EditorState.create({doc, extensions:[…]})`; subsequent doc updates flow via `view.dispatch({changes:{from,to,insert}})`, NOT by re-rendering. Use `EditorView.updateListener.of((u)=>u.docChanged && setCode(u.state.doc.toString()))` to mirror doc into React state.\n23\t- **eslint react-hooks/refs rule is strict.** Never write `someRef.current = value` at component top level — must be inside `useEffect(() => { someRef.current = value; }, [value])` or inside an event handler. Pattern for \"always-fresh closure\" inside a handler set up once: declare `const valueRef = useRef(value); useEffect(() => { valueRef.current = value; }, [value]);` then read `valueRef.current` inside the long-lived closure.\n24\t- **Cmd/Ctrl+Enter in CodeMirror.** Use `keymap.of([{ key: 'Mod-Enter', preventDefault: true, run: () => { ...; return true; } }])` and put it BEFORE the `defaultKeymap` keymap so it wins over Cm-Enter defaults. `Mod` resolves to ⌘ on Mac and Ctrl elsewhere. Have the `run` callback dispatch via a ref (`handleRunRef.current()`) so it always picks up the latest closure.\n25\t- **Progress PATCH for sectionState.** PATCH `/api/progress` with body `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { userCode } } }`. To CLEAR a section's state (e.g. on Reset), send `{ [sectionId]: {} }` — the server's `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into existing `sectionState[sectionId]` then replaces it, so `{}` overwrites and effectively wipes the entry's userCode. Caveat: this also wipes any sibling fields (quizSubmission) on the same section, which is fine because section IDs are per-widget-instance. To mark a section \"done\", PATCH `{ userCode, done: true }` together — `done?: boolean` is the per-section completion flag (added in US-011); sending `{ done: true }` alone would wipe userCode.\n26\t- **CodeRunner slots (US-011).** CodeRunner exposes slot props for graded variants without re-implementing the editor/footer: `extraPanel?: ReactNode` (rendered between output panel and footer), `primaryAction?: { label, icon, onClick, disabled, variant: 'primary'|'secondary'|'ghost', testId, ariaLabel }` (replaces ▶ Run; pass `null` to hide it entirely), `onCodeChange?: (code) => void` (mirror doc into parent state), `onReset?: () => void` (parent can also reset its own state when CodeRunner's Reset fires), `outputPlaceholder?: string`. CodeRunner also exports `codeRunnerEditorTheme` and `codeRunnerHighlightStyle` so child components (e.g. inline read-only test bodies) match the editor's look. Read-only CodeMirror needs BOTH `EditorState.readOnly.of(true)` and `EditorView.editable.of(false)`.\n27\t- **TS target ES2017.** The regex `s` (dotAll) flag triggers `TS1501`. Use `[\\s\\S]` in patterns that need to span newlines, never `/.../s`.\n28\t- **Lesson navigation.** Flat ordered lesson list = `course.modules.flatMap(m => m.lessons)`. Prev/next of current lesson is index-1 / index+1 in that list, crossing module boundaries. Client navigation uses `router.push(\\`/courses/\\${slug}/lessons/\\${targetSlug}\\`)` from `next/navigation`'s `useRouter()`. Mark-finished is `PATCH /api/progress { courseSlug, lessonSlug, status: 'finished' }` — applyProgressPatch already handles this and stamps `finishedAt`.\n29\t- **Adding a new widget type = 5 mandatory wiring points** (see `src/widgets/README.md`): (1) `--widget-<name>` CSS var in both light + dark blocks of `src/styles/tokens.css`; (2) Zod data schema at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts` + register in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` so `npm run build:schemas` emits `<name>.json`; (3) `widgetRegistry` entry in `src/widgets/registry.ts` (component / label / icon / accentVar) + extend the `WidgetType` union; (4) `<Name>Editor.tsx` per US-023 pattern + import + branch in both `WidgetEditPanel` and `SectionRenderer` in `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx`; (5) `<Name>SectionSchema` variant in `SectionSchema` discriminated union at `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts`. Skipping (5) means widget renders but lesson JSON containing it fails API validation. Histogram (US-030) is the canonical reference implementation.\n30\t- **React-aware playwright slider input.** Setting `el.value` directly bypasses React's value tracker — the `onChange` handler sees the *previous* value. Use the native setter override: `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, 'value').set.call(el, '4'); el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));`. Same pattern works for `<select>`, `<textarea>`.\n31\t- **Pyodide lesson namespace + test isolation (US-031).** Worker holds a Python-side module-level dict `__ai_lesson_globals` (sourced from `src/lib/pyodide/runnerPython.ts` so vitest can re-install it via the `pyodide` npm dev-dep). All `'run'` calls exec'd with `runPythonAsync(code, { globals: lessonGlobalsProxy })` so the namespace persists across Code/Sandbox widgets within a lesson; `'runWithTests'` exec's user code in lessonGlobals (so helpers persist) but each test body in `dict(__ai_lesson_globals)` (so test mutations don't leak). `'resetNamespace'` (new message type, payload `{ lessonSlug }`) calls `__ai_reset_namespace()` which `.clear()`s in place — DON'T reassign the dict, the JS-side proxy points at the original object. Lesson page calls `usePyodide().resetNamespace(lessonSlug)` from a `useEffect([lessonSlug])` so the namespace wipes on every lesson navigation; toolbar `[data-testid=\"reset-session-btn\"]` exposes a manual reset with a `[data-testid=\"session-toast\"]` ack.\n32\t- **Browser tests touching Code/Sandbox widgets must clear `~/.ai-lecturer/progress.json` per-section state first.** Persisted `userCode` (from US-011) auto-loads as `initialCode`, so a stale entry from a prior aborted run silently shapes Submit outcomes. Wipe via `node -e` JSON edit or use a throwaway course slug.\n33\t- **CodeMirror typing in playwright auto-indents on `\\n`.** `keyboard.type('def f():\\\\n    return 42\\\\n')` produces compound indents. Use single-line lambdas where possible; otherwise insert `Enter` + `Home` between lines, or paste via `view.dispatch({changes:{...}})`.\n34\t- **Pyodide batched stdout strips `\\n` (US-032).** `setStdout({ batched })` fires once per line, content only — never join chunks with `''` or consecutive `print()`s collapse into one line. Use the `formatStdoutChunks` helper at `src/lib/pyodide/stdout.ts`: joins with `\\n`, then per-line keeps only the substring after the last `\\r` so terminal-style in-place updates work and bare `\\r`s don't render as extra line breaks under `pre-wrap`. The CodeRunner output panel already uses `whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'`, so once newlines actually exist in the text, multi-line output renders correctly.\n35\t- **Worker plot capture (US-045 `runWithPlotParam`).** Matplotlib loaded lazily on first request via `loadPackage(['matplotlib'])` then `matplotlib.use('AGG')` (no display server in worker). Cache namespaces by `setupCode` STRING as the key (`__ai_pexp_namespaces[setup_code]`) so identical setupCode runs once per session — the cached dict is copied with `dict(cached)` for each render so user mutations don't leak. Capture the most-recent figure with `plt.figure(plt.get_fignums()[-1]).savefig(buf, format='png', bbox_inches='tight', dpi=110)` then `plt.close('all')` before the next render. JS plain-object payload (`{name: number|string|boolean}`) crosses the JS→Py boundary as a JsProxy → `params.to_py()` yields a Python dict; types are preserved automatically (number→float, bool→bool, string→str).\n36\t- **Next dev (Turbopack) can hang under back-to-back playwright runs.** Symptom: first navigation succeeds, second test run's `page.goto` times out and `curl` to ANY route hangs indefinitely. Recovery: `pkill -f \"next dev\"` and restart on a different port. Suspect dangling chromium HMR socket from the previous run.\n37\t- **react-hooks/set-state-in-effect rule.** A bare `void asyncFn()` inside `useEffect` triggers this even if setState happens after `await` (the linter doesn't follow async boundaries). Gate the call behind a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag (`if (initialRenderRef.current) return; initialRenderRef.current = true; void asyncFn();`) — the linter sees this as a one-time subscription and accepts it. Same gating pattern that GaussDemo uses with its `pendingSigmaRef` ref-check.\n38\t- **Mark a non-Code section \"done\".** PATCH `/api/progress` with `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }`. `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into `sectionState[sectionId]`, so sibling fields on other sections are untouched. Section IDs are per-widget-instance, so this is the canonical pattern when there's no `userCode` to persist (Quiz, CodeCloze, DragMatch, etc.).\n39\t- **Mixing CSS shorthand `border` with separate `borderColor` re-renders trigger a React style warning.** Don't compose `{ border: '1px solid X' }` with a hover override `{ borderColor: 'Y' }`. Use longhand from the start (`borderWidth`, `borderStyle`, `borderColor`) so hover/feedback states only override the longhand piece. Surfaces this in DragMatch zone/bank styles where hover swaps the colour.\n40\t- **dnd-kit (`@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`) is already in `package.json` (added pre-MVP).** `useSensors(useSensor(PointerSensor, { activationConstraint: { distance: 4 } }), useSensor(KeyboardSensor))` is the canonical sensor set for keyboard-accessible drag widgets. `useDraggable` automatically attaches `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription` — verifying those attributes is enough to prove keyboard sensors are wired without simulating arrow-key navigation in playwright (each ArrowKey only moves 25 px by default and the simulated drag is brittle). For a draggable+droppable bank/zone layout: track `placement: Record<containerId, itemId[]>` with a sentinel `__bank__` id; on `onDragEnd` find the item's source container, splice it out, push into the target. Use `<DragOverlay>` so the drag preview is portal-rendered and unaffected by transforms inside the original layout.\n41\t- **Inline syntax-highlight for cloze-style widgets.** Don't pull in CodeMirror with `Decoration.replace` widgets when the only requirement is \"syntax-highlighted Python with inline editable inputs\" — a small regex-based tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call) inside `<pre>` is enough, and React-managed `<input>`s blur naturally without bridging CM state. CodeCloze's `tokenizePython` is the reference implementation. Use CodeMirror only when the user types into the code itself (Code, Sandbox, ParametricExplorer's Python editors).\n42\t- **Status badge selector for browser tests.** `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` (NOT `data-widget-status`). `StatusBadge` in `src/widgets/Widget.tsx` exposes the value via `data-status`.\n43\t- **`type ComponentType` import for `widgetRegistry[type].component`.** When the lesson page's `SectionRenderer` forwards optional widget-specific props (e.g. `progressKey`, `onComplete`) via the registry, narrow the registry's `ComponentType<{ data?: unknown }>` with a local cast: `widgetRegistry.codeCloze.component as ComponentType<{ data?: unknown; progressKey?: typeof progressKey; onComplete?: () => void }>`. Add `type ComponentType` to the existing `from 'react'` import block in `page.tsx`.\n44\t- **Avoid `useEffect`+`setState` for \"clamp paging index when filter shrinks rows\".** The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule rejects `useEffect(() => setPage(Math.max(0, totalPages-1)))`. Instead, derive a `clampedPage = Math.min(page, totalPages-1)` value during render and use it for slicing/indicator/disabled-state — let `setPage` only flip on actual user click. This keeps the linter happy and removes a redundant render cycle when filters narrow the result set.\n45\t- **Sticky thead inside an `overflow:auto` scroll container.** `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1` on `<thead>` plus a non-transparent `background` on each `<th>` (or on the `<thead>` itself) is enough — no JS needed. Wrap the `<table>` in a `div` with `maxHeight: '60vh'; overflow: auto` so the sticky context is the wrapper rather than the page.\n46\t- **Cross-origin iframe postMessage spying is blocked.** Playwright (Chromium) throws `SecurityError: Blocked a frame with origin \"...\" from accessing a cross-origin frame` if you try to replace methods on `iframe.contentWindow` for a third-party embed (YouTube, Vimeo, etc.). For seek/play verification on cross-origin video embeds, prefer (a) observable side-effects in the parent's DOM/state (e.g. our own `data-active` flips), or (b) routing the test through an HTML5 `<video>` MP4 path where `video.currentTime` IS reachable from the parent and `Object.defineProperty(v, 'currentTime', { get, set, configurable: true })` works. Also: install the descriptor override AFTER reading the post-mount value, otherwise the React `useEffect` initial assignment is lost.\n47\t- **Adding a new media type to course assets** = extend `CONTENT_TYPES` in `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` (one map gates both the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list). Currently supports `.png/.jpg/.jpeg/.svg/.webp/.gif/.mp4/.webm`.\n48\t\n49\t## 2026-05-04 - US-051\n50\t- Updated scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md with a new \"Step 5: Visual Illustrations\" section placed immediately after \"Step 4: Source Research\".\n51\t- Renumbered subsequent steps: Step 5 → Step 6 (Compose), Step 6 → Step 7 (Write+Validate), Step 7 → Step 8 (Stop). Updated The Job overview to add a new step 5 entry. Back-references to Step 4 in the body remain accurate.\n52\t- New section spells out: inline `![alt](url)` images for theory ≥300 chars; Image widget (US-050, type `image`) for hero figures; preferred sources (Wikimedia Commons / public-domain repos / official docs / arxiv); avoided hosts (medium / towardsdatascience / dev.to / personal blogs / Imgur); REQUIRED meaningful alt text; attribution format `Wikimedia Commons, <author>, <license>` + `attribution.url` to Commons file page.\n53\t- Worked example (Median filter) bumped from 4 → 5 sections: theory now includes an inline Wikimedia salt-and-pepper noise image with descriptive alt; new image-widget section \"edge-preservation-figure\" before the quiz, with full alt + caption + Wikimedia attribution. Footer \"Why this lesson works\" updated to describe both visual additions.\n54\t- Validation checklist appended four new items covering inline-image-on-long-theory, meaningful alt text, host avoidlist, and Wikimedia attribution format.\n55\t- Files changed: scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md\n56\t- Quality: `npm run typecheck` passes (clean). `npm run lint` shows 162 errors but they are all pre-existing on the branch (this PR only touches a markdown file — `git diff --name-only HEAD` confirms).\n57\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n58\t  - When a skill update is purely documentation (markdown only), AC almost always says \"Typecheck passes\" not \"Lint passes\" — a no-op markdown change can't move either metric. Don't get distracted trying to fix unrelated lint errors that pre-date the branch.\n59\t  - Renumbering `## Step N` headings means hunting back-references too. `grep -n \"Step [0-9]\" SKILL.md` surfaces them all in one pass; the existing back-references in this file all referred to Step 4 (Source Research), which kept its number, so no follow-up edits were needed.\n60\t  - The Image widget (US-050) was marked `passes: true` in prd.json but the code (src/widgets/Image/, schemas/image.json, registry entry, ImageSectionSchema variant) is NOT in the repo — the US-050 merge commit only landed the orchestrator's progress logs. The `image` section type the SKILL.md now references won't actually validate against `LessonSchema` until US-050's code lands. Worth flagging for the next reviewer / for whoever picks up the next image-needing story.\n61\t  - Worked example URLs: I used realistic-looking Wikimedia Commons URLs (`upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/...`) for both the inline image (Noise_salt_and_pepper.png) and the Image widget (Median_filter_step_edge.png). They follow the canonical Wikimedia URL shape but I did not live-verify the exact filenames exist — the worked example is documentation, not a live asset; if a future agent copies the URLs into a real lesson they should re-verify on Commons.\n62\t---\n63\t\n64\t## 2026-05-04 - US-052\n65\t- Added `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` — sliding side-panel scaffold with header (AI Tutor + X close), scrollable message list with empty-state placeholder, sticky footer composer (autoresize textarea max 6 lines, Stop placeholder, Send button). ⌘+Enter sends; plain Enter inserts newline; Send disabled when textarea is empty/whitespace-only. Send appends a user bubble + canned assistant placeholder bubble (\"Backend not connected — try again after US-053 ships\") and clears the draft.\n66\t- Draft persisted to `localStorage['lessonChatDraft:<courseSlug>:<lessonSlug>']` debounced 200ms via `setTimeout` inside a `useEffect`. Restored on mount/slug change. Cleared on Send.\n67\t- Panel open/closed state persisted to `localStorage['lessonChat-open']`. Hydrated from storage on mount in the same effect that already hydrates `toc-collapsed`.\n68\t- Lesson page wiring: `chatOpen` state is now stateful (was `useState(false)` const-only); ⌘. keyboard shortcut and the toolbar tutor button (`tutor-btn`) both call `toggleChat` which flips state + persists. `closeChat` (used by panel X button) sets `false` + persists.\n69\t- Toolbar tutor button gains an `active` prop on `ToolbarIconBtn`: when on, paints `--accent-subtle` background + `--accent-text`; sets `aria-pressed=\"true\"` and `data-active=\"true\"`. Old `disabled` styling preserved for other buttons.\n70\t- Removed the placeholder `ChatColumn` (\"AI tutor — coming soon\") component — no longer referenced.\n71\t- Animation: existing `transition: 'grid-template-columns 180ms ease, opacity 600ms ease'` on the lesson shell already drives the slide (chatCol toggles 0px ↔ 320px). `prefers-reduced-motion` is honoured globally via `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { *, *::before, *::after { transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; ... } }` in `src/app/globals.css` — covers both the grid-column transition and any inline transitions we'd add.\n72\t- Files changed: src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx (Toolbar wiring, ⌘. shortcut, ChatColumn removed), src/components/LessonChat.tsx (new).\n73\t- Quality: `npm run typecheck` shows the same 2 pre-existing pyodide test errors as before US-052 (unchanged baseline). `npm run lint` matches baseline 910/2318 (no new errors or warnings). Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-052.js`, 23 assertions) passes — covers panel default-closed, tutor-btn enabled, ⌘. open/close, draft persistence + restoration after reload, whitespace-only Send disabled, ⌘+Enter sends, plain Enter newline, X button persists closed state, no console errors. Screenshots at /tmp/US-052-after-send.png and /tmp/US-052-final.png confirm chrome.\n74\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n75\t  - `display: 'none'` panels are not \"visible\" to playwright's default `waitForSelector`. When asserting a panel returned to closed state, use `page.waitForFunction(() => el.getAttribute('data-open') === 'false')` or pass `state: 'attached'` — otherwise the wait times out even though the attribute already flipped (13× resolved-to-hidden in the timeout log is the tell).\n76\t  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` lint rule fires on `setX(dynamicValue)` inside a `useEffect` body but NOT on `setX(literalValue)`. So an `if (stored) setX(stored); else setX('')` pattern triggers the rule on the first branch (dynamic) — but only one disable directive is needed. If you collapse to `setX(stored ?? '')` the rule still fires because the value is dynamic; keep the inline-disable comment.\n77\t  - Existing prefers-reduced-motion handling is global via `globals.css` — there's no `usePrefersReducedMotion` hook in the repo and we don't need one for this story. Inline `transition: ...` styles ARE overridden by the global `transition-duration: 0.01ms !important` rule, so JS-side gating isn't required.\n78\t  - `ToolbarIconBtn`'s old style mixed `border: '1px solid transparent'` shorthand with conditional values. Codebase pattern (per progress.txt note) is to use longhand `borderWidth`/`borderStyle`/`borderColor` so hover/active variants only override the longhand piece — applied here too.\n79\t  - When wiring localStorage hydration on a lesson page, prefer adding to the existing single mount-effect that already hydrates other persisted state (TOC collapse), rather than spawning a second one. Keeps SSR-flash window down to one frame for both keys.\n80\t  - The previous attempt at US-052 (per `scripts/ralph/logs/US-052.last_failure.txt`) implemented the same code, all checks passed, but the agent exited without `git commit` — losing the entire diff. The orchestrator's \"0 commits\" guard caught it. Always commit BEFORE celebrating green tests.\n81\t---\n82\t\n83\t## 2026-05-04 - US-053\n84\t- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts` — server-side connector module with two implementations selectable at first use and cached for the process lifetime: (a) `agentSdkConnector` dynamically `import('@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk')` and iterates the `query()` async stream, accumulating `assistant` text blocks (falls back to the final `result` field if no blocks were yielded); (b) `subprocessConnector` spawns `claude -p \"<prompt>\" --output-format json` via `child_process.spawn`, parses the JSON, and returns `parsed.result`. Selection: `selectConnector()` tries SDK first, falls back to subprocess after a `claude --version` probe; returns `null` when neither works. Subprocess connector enforces a 60s SIGTERM timeout with a 5s SIGKILL grace, both configurable for tests.\n85\t- Added `src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts` — POST handler that validates body via Zod (`courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionId?, message, history?`), invokes the cached connector, returns `{ assistant: string }` on success, `503` with the spec-mandated body `'AI Tutor unavailable: install Claude Code CLI or sign in to Claude Max.'` when no connector is available, and `502` when the connector itself throws.\n86\t- Wired `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` Send button to POST `/api/lesson-chat`. While the request is in flight, a pending assistant bubble renders 3 animated dots (`<TypingDots/>`, keyframes injected via inline `<style>` since globals.css doesn't have a tutor-specific animation). On success the pending bubble swaps to the real text. On 503 (or any non-OK status, or fetch failure), the bubble swaps to a red error variant (new `errorBubbleStyle` using `--danger-*` tokens, falling back to literal hex). The Send button is also disabled while sending. History is built from prior non-pending messages and sent as `history: Array<{role, content}>` per AC, even though the stub prompt assembly ignores it (US-054).\n87\t- Did NOT install `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` because the package's `peerDependencies` declares `zod@^4.0.0` and the codebase pins `zod@3.x` (per Codebase Patterns). The dynamic import in `agentSdkConnector` raises `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` at first use, which `selectConnector` treats as the documented \"package missing\" fallback path. Adding the package later would require either resolving the peer-dep conflict project-wide or pinning it via `--legacy-peer-deps`. Flagged for whoever ships the SDK path.\n88\t- Files changed: src/components/LessonChat.tsx (modified — backend wiring + typing dots + error bubble); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts (new); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts (new); src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts (new); src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts (new).\n89\t- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 190/190 (added 23 new tests in lessonChat — subprocess parsing, non-zero exit, JSON parse error, missing result field, is_error=true, timeout via mocked spawn, spawn-throws path, SDK collects assistant blocks, SDK falls back to result, SDK no-text rejects, SDK is_error rejects, loadSdk rejects (mimics package missing); selection prefers SDK; selection falls back when SDK throws; selection returns null when both fail; selection caches across calls; route 400/200/503/502 handlers). `npm run lint` 162 errors / 24 warnings — same pre-existing baseline as US-052 (no new errors or warnings from this change). Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-053.js`, 8 assertions) passes against the real `claude -p` subprocess: navigates to `/courses/gauss-basics/lessons/wprowadzenie-do-filtrowania`, opens the chat panel, types \"What is this app?\", confirms user bubble + typing dots + assistant bubble within ~30s, checks textarea is cleared, no console errors. Real assistant response excerpt: \"This app is an AI Lecturer — a single-user local web app that delivers interactive AI-generated lessons…\". Screenshots at /tmp/US-053-typing.png and /tmp/US-053-final.png.\n90\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n91\t  - **claude-agent-sdk has a hard zod v4 peer-dep.** Repo pins zod v3 because `zod-to-json-schema` returns `{}` on zod v4 (existing Codebase Patterns note). Dynamic-importing the SDK and treating `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` as a fallback condition keeps both paths viable without forcing a zod bump. If a future story wants the SDK path live, the cleanest fix is probably moving `zod-to-json-schema` calls behind a typed shim and then bumping zod — not `--legacy-peer-deps`, which leaves both versions in the tree and breaks the discriminator-based widget schemas.\n92\t  - **`claude -p \"<prompt>\" --output-format json` payload shape** (verified live in this story): top-level keys include `type: \"result\"`, `subtype: \"success\"|...`, `is_error: boolean`, `result: string` (the assistant text), `duration_ms`, `usage`, `modelUsage`, `permission_denials`, `terminal_reason`. The minimum to extract assistant text is `JSON.parse(stdout).result` after asserting `is_error !== true`. Don't try to read `--output-format stream-json` or per-message blocks; for non-streaming we only need the final `result`.\n93\t  - **Subprocess timeout pattern in node** with both SIGTERM + SIGKILL grace: outer `setTimeout` calls `child.kill('SIGTERM')` and starts an inner `setTimeout` for SIGKILL `killGraceMs` ms later. Inner timer is cleared inside `settle()` to avoid leaking when the process actually exits between SIGTERM and SIGKILL. The `close` event fires after kill regardless of which signal landed. For tests, mock `kill()` to emit the synthetic `close(143)` event back to satisfy the EventEmitter contract.\n94\t  - **Module-level cache for connector selection.** AC says \"selection cached at server boot\" — Next.js App Router has no `onServerStart`, so module-level lazy cache (`let cached: Connector | null | undefined`) hydrated by the first call to `selectConnector()` is the idiomatic equivalent. Export a `_resetConnectorCacheForTesting()` so unit tests don't poison each other across `forceReselect: true` calls.\n95\t  - **vi.spyOn on a re-exported barrel function** (`vi.spyOn(connectorModule, 'selectConnector')`) only intercepts calls that go through the imported symbol, not direct calls inside the module. Because the route handler imports `selectConnector` from `@/lib/lessonChat/connector` and the test imports the same module, the spy works without `vi.mock(...)`. Same pattern as the existing `api.test.ts` — keep the alias path consistent.\n96\t  - **Playwright `run.js` leaves `.temp-execution-<ts>.js` artifacts** in `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/`. Not gitignored; show up as untracked in `git status` after a browser run. Delete them before committing.\n97\t  - **Lesson chat history field is plumbed end-to-end but unused by the prompt assembly stub.** The route accepts `history: Array<{role, content}>` and the connector signature receives it via `ConnectorRequest`, but `assemblePrompt` only uses `message`. Wiring history (and `sectionId` lesson context) into the actual prompt is US-054. Don't drop the history-collection code in the component when working on US-054 — just teach `assemblePrompt` to consume it.\n98\t  - **For UI tags requiring backend, run `npm run dev` then point playwright at it.** Detection helper missed the server initially (per the existing playwright skill note); just hardcode `TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3000/...'` in the test script. The dev server starts cleanly in <300ms with Turbopack.\n99\t---\n100\t\n101\t## 2026-05-04 - US-054\n102\t- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/context.ts` exporting `buildPromptContext({ lesson, currentSectionId? }) → { systemPrompt, contextBlock }`. `systemPrompt` is the spec-mandated string verbatim. `contextBlock` always leads with `Lesson title: …\\nEyebrow: …\\nDescription: …\\nEstimated minutes: …`. When `currentSectionId` resolves to a real section, the active section is serialised per type (theory→`markdown`; quiz→question + numbered options; code→`taskMarkdown` + `starterCode`; codeCloze→`taskMarkdown`+template; sandbox/demo/histogram/plotImage/parametricExplorer/dragMatch/dataTable/video/custom→short type-specific summary). When `currentSectionId` is omitted or unknown, falls back to `Lesson outline:\\n- [<type>] <title>` lines. If the assembled string exceeds `CONTEXT_CHAR_LIMIT` (4000) the body portion is truncated and `'… [truncated]'` appended; the lesson header is preserved.\n103\t- Wired `src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts` to load the lesson via `lessonFile()` + `LessonSchema.parse()`, call `buildPromptContext({ lesson, currentSectionId: req.body.sectionId })`, and pass `{ systemPrompt, userMessage: '<contextBlock>\\n\\nUser question: <message>', history }` to the connector. New 404 path when the lesson file is missing; 500 when stored JSON fails schema.\n104\t- Updated `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts` interface: `ConnectorRequest` now `{ systemPrompt?, userMessage, history? }` (was `{ message, history? }`). Both `subprocessConnector` and `agentSdkConnector` pass `assemblePrompt(req.userMessage, req.systemPrompt)` to the underlying CLI/SDK. `assemblePrompt` retains a default fallback prompt for direct callers/tests.\n105\t- `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` now tracks the active section via IntersectionObserver. Effect runs when `open` flips true; observes every `[data-section-id]` element with `rootMargin: '0px 0px -75% 0px'` so only the strip near the top of the viewport counts as \"active\". Picks the highest-DOM-order intersecting section so when several straddle the band we keep the one the learner has scrolled into. Seeds an initial `activeSectionId` from current scroll position so the first message after opening has a value before IO fires. Wraps in a `MutationObserver` on `document.body` so sections rendered AFTER the panel opens (lesson loads async) get observed too. The fetch POST now includes `sectionId: activeSectionId ?? undefined`. Panel exposes `data-active-section-id={activeSectionId ?? ''}` for tests.\n106\t- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/context.test.ts` (8 tests): systemPrompt verbatim, lesson metadata in contextBlock, theory-section body, quiz question+numbered options, code task+starter, outline fallback when sectionId omitted, outline fallback when sectionId unknown, truncation when content exceeds 4000 chars.\n107\t- Updated `src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts` to write a fake lesson under a `mkdtempSync` `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` so the new disk read works; also added a \"passes systemPrompt + contextBlock-derived userMessage to connector\" test that captures the connector's `chat()` arg and checks for `Lesson title:`, the section markdown, and `User question: <text>` substrings. Plus a 404 case when the lesson file is missing.\n108\t- Updated existing `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts` to use the new `userMessage` field in place of `message`.\n109\t- Files changed: src/lib/lessonChat/context.ts (new); src/lib/lessonChat/context.test.ts (new); src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts (modified — fetches lesson, builds context); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts (modified — ConnectorRequest shape); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts (modified — userMessage); src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts (modified — disk fixture + new assertions); src/components/LessonChat.tsx (modified — IO + MO + sectionId in POST).\n110\t- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 200/200 (added 9 new tests across context.test.ts and route.test.ts). `npm run lint` baseline 163/25 unchanged from US-053. Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-054.js`, 8 assertions) passes against the real `claude -p` subprocess: navigates to seed lesson, opens chat panel, programmatically scrolls main content so quiz section `s2-quiz-kernel` reaches the top, waits for `data-active-section-id` to flip to that id, sends \"What is this question testing?\", confirms POST body includes `sectionId: 's2-quiz-kernel'`, and validates the assistant reply explicitly references the **kernel** quiz topic (\"This question is testing whether you understand the **definition of a kernel** in image filtering — specifically, that it's a small matrix of weights used in the convolution operation.\"). Screenshot at /tmp/US-054-after-send.png.\n111\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n112\t  - **IntersectionObserver vs late-rendering targets.** When the chat panel opens immediately after navigation, the `useEffect` may run before the lesson page has fetched its data and rendered `[data-section-id]` elements. A first-pass `document.querySelectorAll('[data-section-id]')` returns 0. The fix is twofold: (a) observe what's currently mounted, (b) wrap a `MutationObserver` on `document.body` (`{childList: true, subtree: true}`) and re-call `observeAllSections()` on each mutation, with a `WeakSet<Element>` to avoid double-observing. The old \"queryAll once in useEffect\" pattern only works when the parent's content is statically rendered before the effect runs.\n113\t  - **rootMargin trick for \"section-at-the-top\" detection.** `rootMargin: '0px 0px -75% 0px'` shrinks the IntersectionObserver root rect so only the top 25% of the viewport counts as \"intersecting\". Combined with picking the highest-DOM-order intersecting section, you reliably get \"what is the user reading right now\". A naive ratio-based pick gets fooled by big sections (a long theory section with ratio 0.6 wins over a small quiz with ratio 1.0).\n114\t  - **vitest + COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE for route handlers that touch fs.** The lesson-chat route now reads from disk. To test it without polluting `courses/`, snapshot the env var, point it at a `mkdtempSync(...)` dir, write a single fake lesson JSON inside `<root>/<courseSlug>/lessons/<lessonSlug>.json`, and restore the env var in `afterAll`. `assertSafeSlug` in `paths.ts` is happy with the slugs `c` / `l` so the fixture file path is just `<tmp>/c/lessons/l.json`.\n115\t  - **Connector signature is an internal contract — break it freely between US-053 and US-054.** Renaming `ConnectorRequest.message → userMessage` and adding `systemPrompt?` was the cleanest expression of \"the route now owns prompt assembly\". Updating the existing test fixture's `message: 'hi'` → `userMessage: 'hi'` was a one-pass `sed`. Don't try to keep both shapes for backwards compatibility — the connector has exactly one consumer (the API route) so the bridge is invisible.\n116\t  - **Playwright skill `run.js` requires the script to self-wrap.** A `module.exports = async ({ chromium }) => {...}` pattern silently no-ops because the wrapper only auto-wraps inline code; for file mode it just `require()`s the file and assumes the script self-executes. Use the existing US-053 pattern: `const { chromium } = require('playwright'); (async () => { ... })().catch(...)`. The wrapper documents this in the auto-wrap branch only — a script that lacks the `(async () => {` token but has `require(` is run as-is.\n117\t  - **playwright `waitForSelector('...[data-open=\"true\"]')` doesn't poll attribute changes well.** Even when the attribute is set in the same render commit as the element appearing, the visibility check sometimes flakes. Prefer `page.waitForFunction(() => el.getAttribute('data-open') === 'true')` for attribute transitions — same pattern as the US-052 close-state assertion learning.\n118\t  - **Test cleanup matters before browser runs in dev.** localStorage state from the prior US-053 run (`lessonChat-open`, `lessonChatDraft:…`) survives across reloads and test runs because the dev server points at the same origin. The US-054 playwright test removes both keys in-page before the explicit reload, otherwise the chat panel opens unexpectedly and the `tutor-btn` toggle inverts.\n119\t---\n120\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af09fd90-aa43-4e2e-8fd9-839962b1c817","uuid":"444b6259-8d50-471c-b7ab-73586cead051","timestamp":"2026-05-04T06:48:10.372Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-055/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","content":"# Ralph Progress Log\nRotated: Mon May  4 00:43:02 CEST 2026\nPrevious log archived to: archive/progress-2026-05-04-0043.txt\n---\n\n## Codebase Patterns\n- Repo dir is named `US-001` (capitalized) → cannot run `create-next-app .` directly because npm rejects capital letters in package names. Workaround: scaffold into a temp dir (e.g. `/tmp/ai-lecturer-scaffold`), then copy files into the worktree (skip the inner `.git`), and set the package name in `package.json` manually.\n- `shadcn@latest` (v4.x) emits Tailwind v4 / `base-nova` style by default — incompatible with a Tailwind v3 project. Use `shadcn@2.3.0` for v3-compatible init, or write `components.json` by hand.\n- Tailwind v3 baseline = `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;` in `globals.css` + `tailwind.config.ts` with `content: [\"./src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mdx}\"]` + `postcss.config.js` with `tailwindcss` and `autoprefixer` plugins. Theme/token wiring belongs in US-002, not US-001.\n- Design tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css` (canonical source from `claude/design/source/tokens.css`) and are imported at the top of `src/app/globals.css`. Tailwind utilities resolve through CSS vars, so changing a `--*` value at runtime updates Tailwind classes too.\n- Theme/accent/density are switched by `data-theme` / `data-accent` / `data-density` attributes on `<html>` (defaults: `light` / `default` / `comfortable`). Selectors in tokens.css are scoped to `:root[data-theme=…]` etc. — adding new variants means adding a new `:root[data-…=\"…\"]` block, not a new file.\n- Geist Sans + Mono are loaded via `next/font` (`geist/font/sans`, `geist/font/mono`) in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Their `.variable` classNames define `--font-geist-sans` / `--font-geist-mono`; tokens.css references those via `var(--font-geist-sans)` inside `--font-sans` / `--font-prose` / `--font-display`. Don't hardcode font names anywhere else.\n- Playwright skill at `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/` ships without `node_modules`; run `npm install --no-audit --no-fund` inside it before first use. Its `detectDevServers()` helper missed our :3000 dev server even when up — fall back to setting `TARGET_URL` manually in the test script if detection fails.\n- **Zod is pinned to v3** (`^3.25.x`) because `zod-to-json-schema` returns an empty object on Zod v4. Don't bump zod to v4 unless the `zod-to-json-schema` import also changes. (Zod v4 has a native `z.toJSONSchema()`, but our AC mandates the third-party lib.)\n- **Vitest needs its own alias config.** `vitest.config.ts` must declare `resolve.alias = { '@': fileURLToPath(new URL('./src', import.meta.url)) }`. Vitest does NOT read `tsconfig.json#paths`. Next + `tsc` + `tsx` (used by `npm run build:schemas`) DO auto-pick it up.\n- **Eslint config does not exempt `_`-prefixed unused vars.** For \"drop one field\" test fixtures, use `const broken: Partial<typeof obj> = { ...obj }; delete broken.field;` — destructuring with `_name` triggers `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` warnings.\n- **Schema layout.** Source-of-truth Zod schemas live in two places: per-widget data shapes at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts`; everything else (Course, Module, Lesson, Section discriminated union, Progress, CourseSpec) at `src/lib/schemas/`. `SectionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', […])` over `'theory'|'quiz'|'code'|'demo'|'sandbox'|'custom'`. Adding a new widget = new folder under `src/widgets/<Name>/` + register a variant in `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` + add it to the `widgets` map in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts`. `npm run build:schemas` regenerates the committed `*.json` files in `src/widgets/schemas/`.\n- **Filesystem helpers** live in `src/lib/server/` (server-only — never import from a `'use client'` module). `paths.ts` exports `coursesRoot()`, `assertSafeSlug()`, `slugify()`, `courseDir/courseFile/courseSpecFile/lessonFile()`. `atomic.ts` exports `atomicWriteJson(path, data)` (writes to `<path>.tmp` then `fs.rename`). `coursesRoot()` honours `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` env var (used in tests); production reads `path.join(process.cwd(), 'courses')`. Disk layout: `courses/<slug>/{course.json, course-spec.json, lessons/<lessonSlug>.json}`.\n- **Next 16 route handlers + vitest.** Tests can import handlers directly from `src/app/api/.../route.ts` and call them with a synthesised `Request` and `{ params: Promise.resolve({...}) }` (Next 15+ wraps params in a Promise). `NextResponse.json()` returns a real `Response`, so `await res.json()` and `res.status` work in tests. Put the test file OUTSIDE `src/app/` (e.g. `src/lib/server/api.test.ts`) so Next doesn't try to compile it as a route — vitest's `include: 'src/**/*.test.ts'` still picks it up.\n- **Slug rules.** `assertSafeSlug` rejects empty strings and any slug containing `/`, `\\`, or `..` (path-traversal protection). Public slugs are derived from user input via `slugify()` (NFKD-normalise → strip combining marks → lowercase → `[_\\s]+→-` → strip non-`[a-z0-9-]` → collapse `-+` → trim). Slugify can return `''` for all-punctuation inputs; callers must guard (POST `/api/courses` returns 400 in that case).\n- **Pyodide worker singleton.** Web Workers are bundled by Turbopack via `new Worker(new URL('./worker.ts', import.meta.url))` (NO `type: 'module'` → classic worker, can use `importScripts` for CDN bootstrap). The worker file at `src/lib/pyodide/worker.ts` is excluded from main thread imports by virtue of being instantiated only via the URL constructor. Client hook lives at `src/lib/pyodide/client.ts` (`'use client'`) and exposes `usePyodide()`; the worker is a module-scope singleton created lazily on first hook subscription via `useSyncExternalStore`. Subscription on mount = lazy-load contract: dashboards / SSR never trigger worker creation. For id-keyed promise resolution: each `run`/`runWithTests` call generates `req-N`, stores `{resolve, reject}` in a `Map`, and pops on matching `event.data.id`. Custom test runner (no pytest) lives in a Python `__ai_run_tests` function injected once per worker; it `exec()`s each test body in a fresh copy of the user namespace and catches `AssertionError` separately for `assertionDetail`. Test results array shape: `[{name, passed, traceback?, assertionDetail?}]`.\n- **CodeMirror 6 setup.** Packages: `codemirror @codemirror/state @codemirror/view @codemirror/lang-python @codemirror/commands @codemirror/language @codemirror/autocomplete` (commands brings `defaultKeymap`/`history`/`historyKeymap`/`indentWithTab`; language brings `HighlightStyle`/`syntaxHighlighting`/`bracketMatching`/`indentOnInput`). Theme via `EditorView.theme({...})` consuming our `--code-bg/--code-text/--code-keyword/...` CSS vars. Highlight via `HighlightStyle.define([{ tag: t.keyword, color: 'var(--code-keyword)' }, ...])` from `@lezer/highlight` tags. Editor instantiated once in `useEffect(() => {...}, [])` with `EditorState.create({doc, extensions:[…]})`; subsequent doc updates flow via `view.dispatch({changes:{from,to,insert}})`, NOT by re-rendering. Use `EditorView.updateListener.of((u)=>u.docChanged && setCode(u.state.doc.toString()))` to mirror doc into React state.\n- **eslint react-hooks/refs rule is strict.** Never write `someRef.current = value` at component top level — must be inside `useEffect(() => { someRef.current = value; }, [value])` or inside an event handler. Pattern for \"always-fresh closure\" inside a handler set up once: declare `const valueRef = useRef(value); useEffect(() => { valueRef.current = value; }, [value]);` then read `valueRef.current` inside the long-lived closure.\n- **Cmd/Ctrl+Enter in CodeMirror.** Use `keymap.of([{ key: 'Mod-Enter', preventDefault: true, run: () => { ...; return true; } }])` and put it BEFORE the `defaultKeymap` keymap so it wins over Cm-Enter defaults. `Mod` resolves to ⌘ on Mac and Ctrl elsewhere. Have the `run` callback dispatch via a ref (`handleRunRef.current()`) so it always picks up the latest closure.\n- **Progress PATCH for sectionState.** PATCH `/api/progress` with body `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { userCode } } }`. To CLEAR a section's state (e.g. on Reset), send `{ [sectionId]: {} }` — the server's `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into existing `sectionState[sectionId]` then replaces it, so `{}` overwrites and effectively wipes the entry's userCode. Caveat: this also wipes any sibling fields (quizSubmission) on the same section, which is fine because section IDs are per-widget-instance. To mark a section \"done\", PATCH `{ userCode, done: true }` together — `done?: boolean` is the per-section completion flag (added in US-011); sending `{ done: true }` alone would wipe userCode.\n- **CodeRunner slots (US-011).** CodeRunner exposes slot props for graded variants without re-implementing the editor/footer: `extraPanel?: ReactNode` (rendered between output panel and footer), `primaryAction?: { label, icon, onClick, disabled, variant: 'primary'|'secondary'|'ghost', testId, ariaLabel }` (replaces ▶ Run; pass `null` to hide it entirely), `onCodeChange?: (code) => void` (mirror doc into parent state), `onReset?: () => void` (parent can also reset its own state when CodeRunner's Reset fires), `outputPlaceholder?: string`. CodeRunner also exports `codeRunnerEditorTheme` and `codeRunnerHighlightStyle` so child components (e.g. inline read-only test bodies) match the editor's look. Read-only CodeMirror needs BOTH `EditorState.readOnly.of(true)` and `EditorView.editable.of(false)`.\n- **TS target ES2017.** The regex `s` (dotAll) flag triggers `TS1501`. Use `[\\s\\S]` in patterns that need to span newlines, never `/.../s`.\n- **Lesson navigation.** Flat ordered lesson list = `course.modules.flatMap(m => m.lessons)`. Prev/next of current lesson is index-1 / index+1 in that list, crossing module boundaries. Client navigation uses `router.push(\\`/courses/\\${slug}/lessons/\\${targetSlug}\\`)` from `next/navigation`'s `useRouter()`. Mark-finished is `PATCH /api/progress { courseSlug, lessonSlug, status: 'finished' }` — applyProgressPatch already handles this and stamps `finishedAt`.\n- **Adding a new widget type = 5 mandatory wiring points** (see `src/widgets/README.md`): (1) `--widget-<name>` CSS var in both light + dark blocks of `src/styles/tokens.css`; (2) Zod data schema at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts` + register in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` so `npm run build:schemas` emits `<name>.json`; (3) `widgetRegistry` entry in `src/widgets/registry.ts` (component / label / icon / accentVar) + extend the `WidgetType` union; (4) `<Name>Editor.tsx` per US-023 pattern + import + branch in both `WidgetEditPanel` and `SectionRenderer` in `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx`; (5) `<Name>SectionSchema` variant in `SectionSchema` discriminated union at `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts`. Skipping (5) means widget renders but lesson JSON containing it fails API validation. Histogram (US-030) is the canonical reference implementation.\n- **React-aware playwright slider input.** Setting `el.value` directly bypasses React's value tracker — the `onChange` handler sees the *previous* value. Use the native setter override: `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, 'value').set.call(el, '4'); el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));`. Same pattern works for `<select>`, `<textarea>`.\n- **Pyodide lesson namespace + test isolation (US-031).** Worker holds a Python-side module-level dict `__ai_lesson_globals` (sourced from `src/lib/pyodide/runnerPython.ts` so vitest can re-install it via the `pyodide` npm dev-dep). All `'run'` calls exec'd with `runPythonAsync(code, { globals: lessonGlobalsProxy })` so the namespace persists across Code/Sandbox widgets within a lesson; `'runWithTests'` exec's user code in lessonGlobals (so helpers persist) but each test body in `dict(__ai_lesson_globals)` (so test mutations don't leak). `'resetNamespace'` (new message type, payload `{ lessonSlug }`) calls `__ai_reset_namespace()` which `.clear()`s in place — DON'T reassign the dict, the JS-side proxy points at the original object. Lesson page calls `usePyodide().resetNamespace(lessonSlug)` from a `useEffect([lessonSlug])` so the namespace wipes on every lesson navigation; toolbar `[data-testid=\"reset-session-btn\"]` exposes a manual reset with a `[data-testid=\"session-toast\"]` ack.\n- **Browser tests touching Code/Sandbox widgets must clear `~/.ai-lecturer/progress.json` per-section state first.** Persisted `userCode` (from US-011) auto-loads as `initialCode`, so a stale entry from a prior aborted run silently shapes Submit outcomes. Wipe via `node -e` JSON edit or use a throwaway course slug.\n- **CodeMirror typing in playwright auto-indents on `\\n`.** `keyboard.type('def f():\\\\n    return 42\\\\n')` produces compound indents. Use single-line lambdas where possible; otherwise insert `Enter` + `Home` between lines, or paste via `view.dispatch({changes:{...}})`.\n- **Pyodide batched stdout strips `\\n` (US-032).** `setStdout({ batched })` fires once per line, content only — never join chunks with `''` or consecutive `print()`s collapse into one line. Use the `formatStdoutChunks` helper at `src/lib/pyodide/stdout.ts`: joins with `\\n`, then per-line keeps only the substring after the last `\\r` so terminal-style in-place updates work and bare `\\r`s don't render as extra line breaks under `pre-wrap`. The CodeRunner output panel already uses `whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'`, so once newlines actually exist in the text, multi-line output renders correctly.\n- **Worker plot capture (US-045 `runWithPlotParam`).** Matplotlib loaded lazily on first request via `loadPackage(['matplotlib'])` then `matplotlib.use('AGG')` (no display server in worker). Cache namespaces by `setupCode` STRING as the key (`__ai_pexp_namespaces[setup_code]`) so identical setupCode runs once per session — the cached dict is copied with `dict(cached)` for each render so user mutations don't leak. Capture the most-recent figure with `plt.figure(plt.get_fignums()[-1]).savefig(buf, format='png', bbox_inches='tight', dpi=110)` then `plt.close('all')` before the next render. JS plain-object payload (`{name: number|string|boolean}`) crosses the JS→Py boundary as a JsProxy → `params.to_py()` yields a Python dict; types are preserved automatically (number→float, bool→bool, string→str).\n- **Next dev (Turbopack) can hang under back-to-back playwright runs.** Symptom: first navigation succeeds, second test run's `page.goto` times out and `curl` to ANY route hangs indefinitely. Recovery: `pkill -f \"next dev\"` and restart on a different port. Suspect dangling chromium HMR socket from the previous run.\n- **react-hooks/set-state-in-effect rule.** A bare `void asyncFn()` inside `useEffect` triggers this even if setState happens after `await` (the linter doesn't follow async boundaries). Gate the call behind a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag (`if (initialRenderRef.current) return; initialRenderRef.current = true; void asyncFn();`) — the linter sees this as a one-time subscription and accepts it. Same gating pattern that GaussDemo uses with its `pendingSigmaRef` ref-check.\n- **Mark a non-Code section \"done\".** PATCH `/api/progress` with `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }`. `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into `sectionState[sectionId]`, so sibling fields on other sections are untouched. Section IDs are per-widget-instance, so this is the canonical pattern when there's no `userCode` to persist (Quiz, CodeCloze, DragMatch, etc.).\n- **Mixing CSS shorthand `border` with separate `borderColor` re-renders trigger a React style warning.** Don't compose `{ border: '1px solid X' }` with a hover override `{ borderColor: 'Y' }`. Use longhand from the start (`borderWidth`, `borderStyle`, `borderColor`) so hover/feedback states only override the longhand piece. Surfaces this in DragMatch zone/bank styles where hover swaps the colour.\n- **dnd-kit (`@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`) is already in `package.json` (added pre-MVP).** `useSensors(useSensor(PointerSensor, { activationConstraint: { distance: 4 } }), useSensor(KeyboardSensor))` is the canonical sensor set for keyboard-accessible drag widgets. `useDraggable` automatically attaches `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription` — verifying those attributes is enough to prove keyboard sensors are wired without simulating arrow-key navigation in playwright (each ArrowKey only moves 25 px by default and the simulated drag is brittle). For a draggable+droppable bank/zone layout: track `placement: Record<containerId, itemId[]>` with a sentinel `__bank__` id; on `onDragEnd` find the item's source container, splice it out, push into the target. Use `<DragOverlay>` so the drag preview is portal-rendered and unaffected by transforms inside the original layout.\n- **Inline syntax-highlight for cloze-style widgets.** Don't pull in CodeMirror with `Decoration.replace` widgets when the only requirement is \"syntax-highlighted Python with inline editable inputs\" — a small regex-based tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call) inside `<pre>` is enough, and React-managed `<input>`s blur naturally without bridging CM state. CodeCloze's `tokenizePython` is the reference implementation. Use CodeMirror only when the user types into the code itself (Code, Sandbox, ParametricExplorer's Python editors).\n- **Status badge selector for browser tests.** `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` (NOT `data-widget-status`). `StatusBadge` in `src/widgets/Widget.tsx` exposes the value via `data-status`.\n- **`type ComponentType` import for `widgetRegistry[type].component`.** When the lesson page's `SectionRenderer` forwards optional widget-specific props (e.g. `progressKey`, `onComplete`) via the registry, narrow the registry's `ComponentType<{ data?: unknown }>` with a local cast: `widgetRegistry.codeCloze.component as ComponentType<{ data?: unknown; progressKey?: typeof progressKey; onComplete?: () => void }>`. Add `type ComponentType` to the existing `from 'react'` import block in `page.tsx`.\n- **Avoid `useEffect`+`setState` for \"clamp paging index when filter shrinks rows\".** The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule rejects `useEffect(() => setPage(Math.max(0, totalPages-1)))`. Instead, derive a `clampedPage = Math.min(page, totalPages-1)` value during render and use it for slicing/indicator/disabled-state — let `setPage` only flip on actual user click. This keeps the linter happy and removes a redundant render cycle when filters narrow the result set.\n- **Sticky thead inside an `overflow:auto` scroll container.** `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1` on `<thead>` plus a non-transparent `background` on each `<th>` (or on the `<thead>` itself) is enough — no JS needed. Wrap the `<table>` in a `div` with `maxHeight: '60vh'; overflow: auto` so the sticky context is the wrapper rather than the page.\n- **Cross-origin iframe postMessage spying is blocked.** Playwright (Chromium) throws `SecurityError: Blocked a frame with origin \"...\" from accessing a cross-origin frame` if you try to replace methods on `iframe.contentWindow` for a third-party embed (YouTube, Vimeo, etc.). For seek/play verification on cross-origin video embeds, prefer (a) observable side-effects in the parent's DOM/state (e.g. our own `data-active` flips), or (b) routing the test through an HTML5 `<video>` MP4 path where `video.currentTime` IS reachable from the parent and `Object.defineProperty(v, 'currentTime', { get, set, configurable: true })` works. Also: install the descriptor override AFTER reading the post-mount value, otherwise the React `useEffect` initial assignment is lost.\n- **Adding a new media type to course assets** = extend `CONTENT_TYPES` in `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` (one map gates both the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list). Currently supports `.png/.jpg/.jpeg/.svg/.webp/.gif/.mp4/.webm`.\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-051\n- Updated scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md with a new \"Step 5: Visual Illustrations\" section placed immediately after \"Step 4: Source Research\".\n- Renumbered subsequent steps: Step 5 → Step 6 (Compose), Step 6 → Step 7 (Write+Validate), Step 7 → Step 8 (Stop). Updated The Job overview to add a new step 5 entry. Back-references to Step 4 in the body remain accurate.\n- New section spells out: inline `![alt](url)` images for theory ≥300 chars; Image widget (US-050, type `image`) for hero figures; preferred sources (Wikimedia Commons / public-domain repos / official docs / arxiv); avoided hosts (medium / towardsdatascience / dev.to / personal blogs / Imgur); REQUIRED meaningful alt text; attribution format `Wikimedia Commons, <author>, <license>` + `attribution.url` to Commons file page.\n- Worked example (Median filter) bumped from 4 → 5 sections: theory now includes an inline Wikimedia salt-and-pepper noise image with descriptive alt; new image-widget section \"edge-preservation-figure\" before the quiz, with full alt + caption + Wikimedia attribution. Footer \"Why this lesson works\" updated to describe both visual additions.\n- Validation checklist appended four new items covering inline-image-on-long-theory, meaningful alt text, host avoidlist, and Wikimedia attribution format.\n- Files changed: scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` passes (clean). `npm run lint` shows 162 errors but they are all pre-existing on the branch (this PR only touches a markdown file — `git diff --name-only HEAD` confirms).\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - When a skill update is purely documentation (markdown only), AC almost always says \"Typecheck passes\" not \"Lint passes\" — a no-op markdown change can't move either metric. Don't get distracted trying to fix unrelated lint errors that pre-date the branch.\n  - Renumbering `## Step N` headings means hunting back-references too. `grep -n \"Step [0-9]\" SKILL.md` surfaces them all in one pass; the existing back-references in this file all referred to Step 4 (Source Research), which kept its number, so no follow-up edits were needed.\n  - The Image widget (US-050) was marked `passes: true` in prd.json but the code (src/widgets/Image/, schemas/image.json, registry entry, ImageSectionSchema variant) is NOT in the repo — the US-050 merge commit only landed the orchestrator's progress logs. The `image` section type the SKILL.md now references won't actually validate against `LessonSchema` until US-050's code lands. Worth flagging for the next reviewer / for whoever picks up the next image-needing story.\n  - Worked example URLs: I used realistic-looking Wikimedia Commons URLs (`upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/...`) for both the inline image (Noise_salt_and_pepper.png) and the Image widget (Median_filter_step_edge.png). They follow the canonical Wikimedia URL shape but I did not live-verify the exact filenames exist — the worked example is documentation, not a live asset; if a future agent copies the URLs into a real lesson they should re-verify on Commons.\n---\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-052\n- Added `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` — sliding side-panel scaffold with header (AI Tutor + X close), scrollable message list with empty-state placeholder, sticky footer composer (autoresize textarea max 6 lines, Stop placeholder, Send button). ⌘+Enter sends; plain Enter inserts newline; Send disabled when textarea is empty/whitespace-only. Send appends a user bubble + canned assistant placeholder bubble (\"Backend not connected — try again after US-053 ships\") and clears the draft.\n- Draft persisted to `localStorage['lessonChatDraft:<courseSlug>:<lessonSlug>']` debounced 200ms via `setTimeout` inside a `useEffect`. Restored on mount/slug change. Cleared on Send.\n- Panel open/closed state persisted to `localStorage['lessonChat-open']`. Hydrated from storage on mount in the same effect that already hydrates `toc-collapsed`.\n- Lesson page wiring: `chatOpen` state is now stateful (was `useState(false)` const-only); ⌘. keyboard shortcut and the toolbar tutor button (`tutor-btn`) both call `toggleChat` which flips state + persists. `closeChat` (used by panel X button) sets `false` + persists.\n- Toolbar tutor button gains an `active` prop on `ToolbarIconBtn`: when on, paints `--accent-subtle` background + `--accent-text`; sets `aria-pressed=\"true\"` and `data-active=\"true\"`. Old `disabled` styling preserved for other buttons.\n- Removed the placeholder `ChatColumn` (\"AI tutor — coming soon\") component — no longer referenced.\n- Animation: existing `transition: 'grid-template-columns 180ms ease, opacity 600ms ease'` on the lesson shell already drives the slide (chatCol toggles 0px ↔ 320px). `prefers-reduced-motion` is honoured globally via `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { *, *::before, *::after { transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; ... } }` in `src/app/globals.css` — covers both the grid-column transition and any inline transitions we'd add.\n- Files changed: src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx (Toolbar wiring, ⌘. shortcut, ChatColumn removed), src/components/LessonChat.tsx (new).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` shows the same 2 pre-existing pyodide test errors as before US-052 (unchanged baseline). `npm run lint` matches baseline 910/2318 (no new errors or warnings). Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-052.js`, 23 assertions) passes — covers panel default-closed, tutor-btn enabled, ⌘. open/close, draft persistence + restoration after reload, whitespace-only Send disabled, ⌘+Enter sends, plain Enter newline, X button persists closed state, no console errors. Screenshots at /tmp/US-052-after-send.png and /tmp/US-052-final.png confirm chrome.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - `display: 'none'` panels are not \"visible\" to playwright's default `waitForSelector`. When asserting a panel returned to closed state, use `page.waitForFunction(() => el.getAttribute('data-open') === 'false')` or pass `state: 'attached'` — otherwise the wait times out even though the attribute already flipped (13× resolved-to-hidden in the timeout log is the tell).\n  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` lint rule fires on `setX(dynamicValue)` inside a `useEffect` body but NOT on `setX(literalValue)`. So an `if (stored) setX(stored); else setX('')` pattern triggers the rule on the first branch (dynamic) — but only one disable directive is needed. If you collapse to `setX(stored ?? '')` the rule still fires because the value is dynamic; keep the inline-disable comment.\n  - Existing prefers-reduced-motion handling is global via `globals.css` — there's no `usePrefersReducedMotion` hook in the repo and we don't need one for this story. Inline `transition: ...` styles ARE overridden by the global `transition-duration: 0.01ms !important` rule, so JS-side gating isn't required.\n  - `ToolbarIconBtn`'s old style mixed `border: '1px solid transparent'` shorthand with conditional values. Codebase pattern (per progress.txt note) is to use longhand `borderWidth`/`borderStyle`/`borderColor` so hover/active variants only override the longhand piece — applied here too.\n  - When wiring localStorage hydration on a lesson page, prefer adding to the existing single mount-effect that already hydrates other persisted state (TOC collapse), rather than spawning a second one. Keeps SSR-flash window down to one frame for both keys.\n  - The previous attempt at US-052 (per `scripts/ralph/logs/US-052.last_failure.txt`) implemented the same code, all checks passed, but the agent exited without `git commit` — losing the entire diff. The orchestrator's \"0 commits\" guard caught it. Always commit BEFORE celebrating green tests.\n---\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-053\n- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts` — server-side connector module with two implementations selectable at first use and cached for the process lifetime: (a) `agentSdkConnector` dynamically `import('@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk')` and iterates the `query()` async stream, accumulating `assistant` text blocks (falls back to the final `result` field if no blocks were yielded); (b) `subprocessConnector` spawns `claude -p \"<prompt>\" --output-format json` via `child_process.spawn`, parses the JSON, and returns `parsed.result`. Selection: `selectConnector()` tries SDK first, falls back to subprocess after a `claude --version` probe; returns `null` when neither works. Subprocess connector enforces a 60s SIGTERM timeout with a 5s SIGKILL grace, both configurable for tests.\n- Added `src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts` — POST handler that validates body via Zod (`courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionId?, message, history?`), invokes the cached connector, returns `{ assistant: string }` on success, `503` with the spec-mandated body `'AI Tutor unavailable: install Claude Code CLI or sign in to Claude Max.'` when no connector is available, and `502` when the connector itself throws.\n- Wired `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` Send button to POST `/api/lesson-chat`. While the request is in flight, a pending assistant bubble renders 3 animated dots (`<TypingDots/>`, keyframes injected via inline `<style>` since globals.css doesn't have a tutor-specific animation). On success the pending bubble swaps to the real text. On 503 (or any non-OK status, or fetch failure), the bubble swaps to a red error variant (new `errorBubbleStyle` using `--danger-*` tokens, falling back to literal hex). The Send button is also disabled while sending. History is built from prior non-pending messages and sent as `history: Array<{role, content}>` per AC, even though the stub prompt assembly ignores it (US-054).\n- Did NOT install `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` because the package's `peerDependencies` declares `zod@^4.0.0` and the codebase pins `zod@3.x` (per Codebase Patterns). The dynamic import in `agentSdkConnector` raises `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` at first use, which `selectConnector` treats as the documented \"package missing\" fallback path. Adding the package later would require either resolving the peer-dep conflict project-wide or pinning it via `--legacy-peer-deps`. Flagged for whoever ships the SDK path.\n- Files changed: src/components/LessonChat.tsx (modified — backend wiring + typing dots + error bubble); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts (new); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts (new); src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts (new); src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts (new).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 190/190 (added 23 new tests in lessonChat — subprocess parsing, non-zero exit, JSON parse error, missing result field, is_error=true, timeout via mocked spawn, spawn-throws path, SDK collects assistant blocks, SDK falls back to result, SDK no-text rejects, SDK is_error rejects, loadSdk rejects (mimics package missing); selection prefers SDK; selection falls back when SDK throws; selection returns null when both fail; selection caches across calls; route 400/200/503/502 handlers). `npm run lint` 162 errors / 24 warnings — same pre-existing baseline as US-052 (no new errors or warnings from this change). Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-053.js`, 8 assertions) passes against the real `claude -p` subprocess: navigates to `/courses/gauss-basics/lessons/wprowadzenie-do-filtrowania`, opens the chat panel, types \"What is this app?\", confirms user bubble + typing dots + assistant bubble within ~30s, checks textarea is cleared, no console errors. Real assistant response excerpt: \"This app is an AI Lecturer — a single-user local web app that delivers interactive AI-generated lessons…\". Screenshots at /tmp/US-053-typing.png and /tmp/US-053-final.png.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - **claude-agent-sdk has a hard zod v4 peer-dep.** Repo pins zod v3 because `zod-to-json-schema` returns `{}` on zod v4 (existing Codebase Patterns note). Dynamic-importing the SDK and treating `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` as a fallback condition keeps both paths viable without forcing a zod bump. If a future story wants the SDK path live, the cleanest fix is probably moving `zod-to-json-schema` calls behind a typed shim and then bumping zod — not `--legacy-peer-deps`, which leaves both versions in the tree and breaks the discriminator-based widget schemas.\n  - **`claude -p \"<prompt>\" --output-format json` payload shape** (verified live in this story): top-level keys include `type: \"result\"`, `subtype: \"success\"|...`, `is_error: boolean`, `result: string` (the assistant text), `duration_ms`, `usage`, `modelUsage`, `permission_denials`, `terminal_reason`. The minimum to extract assistant text is `JSON.parse(stdout).result` after asserting `is_error !== true`. Don't try to read `--output-format stream-json` or per-message blocks; for non-streaming we only need the final `result`.\n  - **Subprocess timeout pattern in node** with both SIGTERM + SIGKILL grace: outer `setTimeout` calls `child.kill('SIGTERM')` and starts an inner `setTimeout` for SIGKILL `killGraceMs` ms later. Inner timer is cleared inside `settle()` to avoid leaking when the process actually exits between SIGTERM and SIGKILL. The `close` event fires after kill regardless of which signal landed. For tests, mock `kill()` to emit the synthetic `close(143)` event back to satisfy the EventEmitter contract.\n  - **Module-level cache for connector selection.** AC says \"selection cached at server boot\" — Next.js App Router has no `onServerStart`, so module-level lazy cache (`let cached: Connector | null | undefined`) hydrated by the first call to `selectConnector()` is the idiomatic equivalent. Export a `_resetConnectorCacheForTesting()` so unit tests don't poison each other across `forceReselect: true` calls.\n  - **vi.spyOn on a re-exported barrel function** (`vi.spyOn(connectorModule, 'selectConnector')`) only intercepts calls that go through the imported symbol, not direct calls inside the module. Because the route handler imports `selectConnector` from `@/lib/lessonChat/connector` and the test imports the same module, the spy works without `vi.mock(...)`. Same pattern as the existing `api.test.ts` — keep the alias path consistent.\n  - **Playwright `run.js` leaves `.temp-execution-<ts>.js` artifacts** in `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/`. Not gitignored; show up as untracked in `git status` after a browser run. Delete them before committing.\n  - **Lesson chat history field is plumbed end-to-end but unused by the prompt assembly stub.** The route accepts `history: Array<{role, content}>` and the connector signature receives it via `ConnectorRequest`, but `assemblePrompt` only uses `message`. Wiring history (and `sectionId` lesson context) into the actual prompt is US-054. Don't drop the history-collection code in the component when working on US-054 — just teach `assemblePrompt` to consume it.\n  - **For UI tags requiring backend, run `npm run dev` then point playwright at it.** Detection helper missed the server initially (per the existing playwright skill note); just hardcode `TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3000/...'` in the test script. The dev server starts cleanly in <300ms with Turbopack.\n---\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-054\n- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/context.ts` exporting `buildPromptContext({ lesson, currentSectionId? }) → { systemPrompt, contextBlock }`. `systemPrompt` is the spec-mandated string verbatim. `contextBlock` always leads with `Lesson title: …\\nEyebrow: …\\nDescription: …\\nEstimated minutes: …`. When `currentSectionId` resolves to a real section, the active section is serialised per type (theory→`markdown`; quiz→question + numbered options; code→`taskMarkdown` + `starterCode`; codeCloze→`taskMarkdown`+template; sandbox/demo/histogram/plotImage/parametricExplorer/dragMatch/dataTable/video/custom→short type-specific summary). When `currentSectionId` is omitted or unknown, falls back to `Lesson outline:\\n- [<type>] <title>` lines. If the assembled string exceeds `CONTEXT_CHAR_LIMIT` (4000) the body portion is truncated and `'… [truncated]'` appended; the lesson header is preserved.\n- Wired `src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts` to load the lesson via `lessonFile()` + `LessonSchema.parse()`, call `buildPromptContext({ lesson, currentSectionId: req.body.sectionId })`, and pass `{ systemPrompt, userMessage: '<contextBlock>\\n\\nUser question: <message>', history }` to the connector. New 404 path when the lesson file is missing; 500 when stored JSON fails schema.\n- Updated `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts` interface: `ConnectorRequest` now `{ systemPrompt?, userMessage, history? }` (was `{ message, history? }`). Both `subprocessConnector` and `agentSdkConnector` pass `assemblePrompt(req.userMessage, req.systemPrompt)` to the underlying CLI/SDK. `assemblePrompt` retains a default fallback prompt for direct callers/tests.\n- `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` now tracks the active section via IntersectionObserver. Effect runs when `open` flips true; observes every `[data-section-id]` element with `rootMargin: '0px 0px -75% 0px'` so only the strip near the top of the viewport counts as \"active\". Picks the highest-DOM-order intersecting section so when several straddle the band we keep the one the learner has scrolled into. Seeds an initial `activeSectionId` from current scroll position so the first message after opening has a value before IO fires. Wraps in a `MutationObserver` on `document.body` so sections rendered AFTER the panel opens (lesson loads async) get observed too. The fetch POST now includes `sectionId: activeSectionId ?? undefined`. Panel exposes `data-active-section-id={activeSectionId ?? ''}` for tests.\n- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/context.test.ts` (8 tests): systemPrompt verbatim, lesson metadata in contextBlock, theory-section body, quiz question+numbered options, code task+starter, outline fallback when sectionId omitted, outline fallback when sectionId unknown, truncation when content exceeds 4000 chars.\n- Updated `src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts` to write a fake lesson under a `mkdtempSync` `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` so the new disk read works; also added a \"passes systemPrompt + contextBlock-derived userMessage to connector\" test that captures the connector's `chat()` arg and checks for `Lesson title:`, the section markdown, and `User question: <text>` substrings. Plus a 404 case when the lesson file is missing.\n- Updated existing `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts` to use the new `userMessage` field in place of `message`.\n- Files changed: src/lib/lessonChat/context.ts (new); src/lib/lessonChat/context.test.ts (new); src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts (modified — fetches lesson, builds context); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts (modified — ConnectorRequest shape); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts (modified — userMessage); src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts (modified — disk fixture + new assertions); src/components/LessonChat.tsx (modified — IO + MO + sectionId in POST).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 200/200 (added 9 new tests across context.test.ts and route.test.ts). `npm run lint` baseline 163/25 unchanged from US-053. Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-054.js`, 8 assertions) passes against the real `claude -p` subprocess: navigates to seed lesson, opens chat panel, programmatically scrolls main content so quiz section `s2-quiz-kernel` reaches the top, waits for `data-active-section-id` to flip to that id, sends \"What is this question testing?\", confirms POST body includes `sectionId: 's2-quiz-kernel'`, and validates the assistant reply explicitly references the **kernel** quiz topic (\"This question is testing whether you understand the **definition of a kernel** in image filtering — specifically, that it's a small matrix of weights used in the convolution operation.\"). Screenshot at /tmp/US-054-after-send.png.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - **IntersectionObserver vs late-rendering targets.** When the chat panel opens immediately after navigation, the `useEffect` may run before the lesson page has fetched its data and rendered `[data-section-id]` elements. A first-pass `document.querySelectorAll('[data-section-id]')` returns 0. The fix is twofold: (a) observe what's currently mounted, (b) wrap a `MutationObserver` on `document.body` (`{childList: true, subtree: true}`) and re-call `observeAllSections()` on each mutation, with a `WeakSet<Element>` to avoid double-observing. The old \"queryAll once in useEffect\" pattern only works when the parent's content is statically rendered before the effect runs.\n  - **rootMargin trick for \"section-at-the-top\" detection.** `rootMargin: '0px 0px -75% 0px'` shrinks the IntersectionObserver root rect so only the top 25% of the viewport counts as \"intersecting\". Combined with picking the highest-DOM-order intersecting section, you reliably get \"what is the user reading right now\". A naive ratio-based pick gets fooled by big sections (a long theory section with ratio 0.6 wins over a small quiz with ratio 1.0).\n  - **vitest + COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE for route handlers that touch fs.** The lesson-chat route now reads from disk. To test it without polluting `courses/`, snapshot the env var, point it at a `mkdtempSync(...)` dir, write a single fake lesson JSON inside `<root>/<courseSlug>/lessons/<lessonSlug>.json`, and restore the env var in `afterAll`. `assertSafeSlug` in `paths.ts` is happy with the slugs `c` / `l` so the fixture file path is just `<tmp>/c/lessons/l.json`.\n  - **Connector signature is an internal contract — break it freely between US-053 and US-054.** Renaming `ConnectorRequest.message → userMessage` and adding `systemPrompt?` was the cleanest expression of \"the route now owns prompt assembly\". Updating the existing test fixture's `message: 'hi'` → `userMessage: 'hi'` was a one-pass `sed`. Don't try to keep both shapes for backwards compatibility — the connector has exactly one consumer (the API route) so the bridge is invisible.\n  - **Playwright skill `run.js` requires the script to self-wrap.** A `module.exports = async ({ chromium }) => {...}` pattern silently no-ops because the wrapper only auto-wraps inline code; for file mode it just `require()`s the file and assumes the script self-executes. Use the existing US-053 pattern: `const { chromium } = require('playwright'); (async () => { ... })().catch(...)`. The wrapper documents this in the auto-wrap branch only — a script that lacks the `(async () => {` token but has `require(` is run as-is.\n  - **playwright `waitForSelector('...[data-open=\"true\"]')` doesn't poll attribute changes well.** Even when the attribute is set in the same render commit as the element appearing, the visibility check sometimes flakes. Prefer `page.waitForFunction(() => el.getAttribute('data-open') === 'true')` for attribute transitions — same pattern as the US-052 close-state assertion learning.\n  - **Test cleanup matters before browser runs in dev.** localStorage state from the prior US-053 run (`lessonChat-open`, `lessonChatDraft:…`) survives across reloads and test runs because the dev server points at the same origin. The US-054 playwright test removes both keys in-page before the explicit reload, otherwise the chat panel opens unexpectedly and the `tutor-btn` toggle inverts.\n---\n","numLines":120,"startLine":1,"totalLines":120}}}
