{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01X61Zv56Sf1SKK5T9NY31B4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QVDaDQdWLHkpTe9GnrANXc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> scripts/ralph/progress.txt <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-055\n- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/inflight.ts` — module-level `Map<requestId, AbortController>` registry plus `register/unregister/abortInflight` helpers and test utilities. Streaming POST registers an entry; the matching DELETE looks it up and calls `.abort()`. Entries are removed on stream end (success, error, or client-disconnect via the ReadableStream's `cancel` callback) so the map can't leak.\n- Extended `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts` `Connector` interface with `chatStream(req, signal): AsyncIterable<ChatStreamEvent>` (event types: `token{text}`, `done`, `error{message}`). Subprocess implementation spawns `claude -p \"<prompt>\"` (NO `--output-format json` — raw streaming text) and emits each newline-terminated stdout line as a `token` event; on close emits `done` (or `error` for non-zero exit). On signal abort: SIGTERM → SIGKILL after `killGraceMs` and the generator returns without `done` so the route can emit a final `aborted` SSE event. SDK implementation iterates `sdk.query({prompt})` and emits each `assistant` content text block as a `token` event; falls back to the `result` field if no blocks were yielded; aborts cooperatively when `signal.aborted` flips.\n- Extended `src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts` POST to inspect `Accept: text/event-stream`. When present, returns a `ReadableStream` that: (1) sends the spec-mandated FIRST event `event: meta\\ndata: {\"requestId\":\"<uuid>\"}\\n\\n` so the client knows what to DELETE, (2) iterates `connector.chatStream(args, abortController.signal)` and re-emits `token`/`done`/`error` events, (3) on signal abort emits a final `aborted` event before closing. The non-SSE JSON path is preserved as-is for the non-streaming consumers (existing tests). The `extract+resolve` lesson-loading path was hoisted into a `resolveRequest` helper so both code paths share validation/file-loading logic without duplication.\n- Added `src/app/api/lesson-chat/[requestId]/route.ts` — DELETE handler that calls `abortInflight(requestId)`. Returns 204 on success, 404 if no inflight entry was found.\n- Updated `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` Send flow to fetch with `Accept: text/event-stream`, read the body via `getReader()` + `TextDecoder`, parse SSE blocks (split on `\\n\\n`, then per-line `event:` / `data:` parsing), and:\n  - Track per-request `AbortController` (`streamAbortRef`) and `requestId` (`currentRequestIdRef`).\n  - On each `token` event, append `obj.text` to a local `accumulated` string and `setMessages` so the assistant bubble updates in real time.\n  - On Stop click: flip a `userStoppedRef`, call `abortController.abort()` (kills the fetch reader), and best-effort `DELETE /api/lesson-chat/<requestId>` (server-side cancel; failures swallowed because the client-side abort already finalised the bubble).\n  - On stream end (or abort with `userStoppedRef.current === true`): set the bubble's `stopped: true` flag and freeze its text to `accumulated`. The bubble renders the partial text + a `<span>` with `STOPPED_SUFFIX = \"— stopped by user\"` styled `fontStyle: italic; color: var(--text-tertiary); display: block` (its own line).\n  - Stop button is now `disabled={!sending}` with an active-state style (border-strong + bg-base + text-base, cursor: pointer); pre-existing `stopBtnStyle` retained for the disabled state.\n  - TypingDots no longer embed a `<style>` keyframes tag inside the bubble; the keyframes are hoisted to a single `<style>` directly inside `<aside>` so they don't pollute `textContent` when tests read the bubble.\n- Added/extended tests:\n  - `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts`: 5 new tests — `subprocessConnector.chatStream` line-by-line tokenisation + `done`, abort kills child without `done`, non-zero exit → `error`; `agentSdkConnector.chatStream` token + done, abort stops mid-stream.\n  - `src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts`: 4 new tests — SSE returns 200 + `text/event-stream` content-type + meta+token+done events; SSE registers requestId and DELETE aborts the in-flight signal (verifies `_inflightSizeForTesting()` returns 0 after); DELETE 404 for unknown requestId; SSE 503 fallback when no connector. Helper `fakeConnector(chatImpl, streamImpl?)` produces a typed `Connector` for spies.\n- Files changed: src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts (chatStream impls); src/lib/lessonChat/inflight.ts (new); src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts (SSE branch + resolveRequest helper); src/app/api/lesson-chat/[requestId]/route.ts (new); src/components/LessonChat.tsx (streaming + Stop wiring + suffix styling); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts (5 new tests); src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts (4 new tests + fakeConnector helper).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 209/209 (added 9 tests; no existing tests changed in behaviour, only mock shapes adapted to the new interface). `npm run lint` 162 errors / 24 warnings (= US-054 baseline 163/25 minus 1 of each — all changes are clean; the dropped pair is an `Unused eslint-disable` directive that no longer fires because adjacent code shifted). Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-055.js`, 12 assertions) passes against the real `claude -p` subprocess: panel opens, Stop initially disabled, partial text streams in (1095 chars before stop), Stop becomes enabled mid-stream, click Stop → bubble flips to `data-stopped=\"true\"` with the partial text PLUS the italic suffix on its own line (1113 chars total, suffix is `display: block; font-style: italic`), Stop disabled after stream ended, follow-up question replies normally (\"2 + 2 = 4. …\"). Screenshot at /tmp/US-055-after-stop.png.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - **Inline `<style>` tags inside repeating React subtrees pollute `textContent`.** TypingDots originally rendered `<style>{keyframes}</style>` inside its own span. The CSS string (~140 chars) was visible to `el.textContent` reads — making playwright's \"wait until bubble has > N chars\" check pass against the keyframes, NOT actual streamed tokens. Hoist single-instance keyframes to the panel root (or a non-text region) so element textContent reflects ONLY the user-visible string. Same trap applies to `<script>` tags.\n  - **`claude -p \"<prompt>\"` (no `--output-format`) streams raw assistant text to stdout.** Each newline-terminated chunk is one paragraph/code-fence/list-line; total stream completes on process exit. For SSE we read line-by-line via `child.stdout.on('data', ...)` + buffer-and-split, NOT via `--output-format stream-json` (which emits per-message JSON envelopes and complicates parsing for what is essentially a passthrough).\n  - **Two-channel cancel: client AbortController + server DELETE.** The Stop button does BOTH. `ac.abort()` on the client ends fetch reading immediately so the bubble freezes. `DELETE /api/lesson-chat/<requestId>` reaches across and kills the subprocess (or aborts the SDK iterator). Without DELETE, the server keeps the subprocess alive draining stdout into a closed stream until the OS reclaims it. Without ac.abort(), the client keeps draining and might process tokens that arrive AFTER the user clicked Stop. Both are necessary; neither alone is correct.\n  - **Map<requestId, AbortController> in module scope IS the canonical \"in-flight registry\" for Next.js App Router.** No global server context exists; module-level state is the equivalent of a process-wide singleton (it's per-route-handler-module but Node only loads each module once per dev/prod server). Always wire a `_resetInflightForTesting()` so tests are deterministic — vitest workers share the module too.\n  - **AbortController wired through ReadableStream's `cancel` callback handles client disconnect.** When the client closes the SSE connection (browser navigation, fetch abort, network drop), the runtime invokes `cancel()` on the ReadableStream. We call `abortController.abort()` + `unregisterInflight(requestId)` from there. This catches the case where the client never sent DELETE (e.g. tab close, Wi-Fi drop) — no leaked subprocess.\n  - **SSE message frame parsing in TypeScript.** Frames are separated by `\\n\\n`. Each frame has lines starting with `event:` / `data:` / `id:` / `retry:` / `:` (comment). For our use, we only need `event:` and `data:`. Multiple `data:` lines in the same frame are joined with `\\n` (per spec). Always `decoder.decode(value, { stream: true })` so multi-byte UTF-8 spanning chunks doesn't break, then a final `decoder.decode()` after the loop to flush the last partial sequence. Same pattern any token-streaming UI in this repo can adopt.\n  - **`accumulated` closure-variable pattern for streaming setState.** Rather than reading-then-writing React state in each token handler, keep a local `let accumulated = ''` in the async closure, increment it sync, and call `setMessages(prev => ...)` with a snapshot. Reading state inside an async callback would race against React's batched updates; the local var is the source of truth for \"what tokens have we received so far\" and gets passed to `finalizeStopped`/the post-loop terminal `setMessages` once.\n  - **Typed `Connector` interface gotcha for `vi.spyOn` mocks.** Adding `chatStream` to `Connector` broke every existing spy that returned `{ name, chat }`. Test helper `fakeConnector(chatImpl, streamImpl?)` papers over this by defaulting `chatStream` to a single-token-then-done generator built from `chat`. Adopt a similar helper any time the Connector contract grows so the existing spies stay one-line.\n  - **Don't put debug `console.log` near token streaming in playwright tests UNLESS you also ingest them in the test.** I added `[chat-debug]` lines in the component, then teaches the playwright `page.on('console')` listener to surface them — that's how I noticed the TypingDots-textContent bug (catch path ran with `accumulated.length=0` even though the bubble seemed to have 142 chars of content).\n---\nEOF\necho \"appended\"","description":"Append progress log entry"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":177245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":566},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af09fd90-aa43-4e2e-8fd9-839962b1c817","uuid":"c0223425-7ec8-4d73-b942-027b65ef11cd"}
